[00:04.66] <Lord, I ain't asking for much>
[00:15.34] <Just help me get out of this chair without making noises>
[00:34.16] <Dear Lord, I got a little request>
[00:38.42] <Nothing fancy, nothing blessed. Just let me find my glasses today>
[00:45.00] <before I buy another pair anyway>
[00:54.34] <And if you could help my memory too>
[00:58.54] <I'd surely appreciate that from you>
[01:01.92] <'Cause I walked into this room just now>
[01:06.20] <and forgot exactly why somehow>
[01:13.14] <Lord, I've got a funny prayer>
[01:17.92] <These old bones could use some grace>
[01:26.78] <My knees sound like a rusty gate>
[01:34.08] <Every time I leave my place>
[01:40.36] <I ain't asking to be twenty>
[01:46.24] <I've already survived that mess>
[01:54.40] <Funny prayer about getting old>
[02:00.74] <Just help me age a little less>
[02:09.06] <Mmmmm>
[02:15.90] <Lord, another thing before I go>
[02:19.78] <Why's every chair so darn low>
[02:23.64] <And who moved the floor so far away>
[02:27.94] <It wasn't like this yesterday>
[02:33.00] <My back writes complaints every morning, before the rooster starts performing>
[02:40.28] <But somehow after coffee's brewed, life>
[02:45.22] <don't seem quite so rude>
[02:49.44] <Lord, I've got a funny prayer>
[02:54.40] <Don't make me young, don't change a thing>
[03:01.22] <Just help me remember>
[03:03.10] <people's names, and where I put my keys again>
[03:10.64] <A little patience for my creaking, and wisdom for what's>
[03:16.74] <coming next>
[03:21.48] <Funny prayer about getting old>
[03:28.10] <That's about all I request>
[03:33.74] <Funny thing about these later years, you laugh more than you used to>
[03:40.48] <'Cause if you don't laugh at getting old, getting old might laugh at you>
[03:46.52] <Lord, I've got a funny prayer>
[03:50.80] <for every soul that's growing gray. May we keep our sense of humor, when our hair decides to stray>
[04:05.34] <May we still enjoy the sunrise, and every day we're still blessed>
[04:16.18] <Funny prayer about getting old>
[04:22.24] <And thank you for the rest>
[04:30.66] <And Lord, if you know where I left my glasses, I'd appreciate a>
[04:39.58] <hint>